Maintainer: Wilson Lara-Henao <wilarhen@gmail.com>
Description: Processes multilevel ecological data series (MEDS)
    arranged in temporal or spatial hierarchies defined by sampling
    designs. The package recursively applies one-level stage functions to
    long-format tree-ring and climate data, then optionally fits a
    terminal model to the processed series. Terminal fits currently
    include mixed-effects detrending through 'nlme' and Friedman
    supersmoother detrending through supsmu() of 'stats'. The package also
    supports post-detrending comparison and inference tools for
    multilevel dendroclimatic analyses. The method is described in
    Lara et al. (2018) <doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0196923>.
